From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zak Peirce <plastikman@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 09:32:53 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] PC5: a refused reservation names what holds the range (Wine
 patch 0983)

prospero-win df3e85f (#737), after the v0.2.0 PC5 builds on, picked onto
PC5's patches.

sceKernelReserveVirtualRange() answers ENOMEM (0x8002000c) both for a range
another mapping holds and for one it cannot grant, so its return code does not
say which, while anon_mmap_tryfixed()'s callers need EEXIST for a collision in
either case: map_view relocates on it and reserve_area skips the block. The
errno is left alone and the cause is logged instead, through the query
structure native/wine64_main.c already declares.

At a fixed base the distinction is the whole diagnosis. 0130 notes that the
title's own image may occupy a program's preferred base and relocates the
program when it does; an image whose relocations were stripped at link time
cannot be relocated and must have that base, and today it fails with
STATUS_CONFLICTING_ADDRESSES with nothing saying whether the base was taken or
the address space was exhausted.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SLRg9a2FLR6N3VhHWuegKB

